00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.160
I work at GSK.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.780
And I work within the
biostatistics space.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.290
And one of the main
roles right now

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.810
that you see across
a lot of pharma

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:02.260
are pharma moving
into the R space

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:05.320
and starting to use
R as a primary tool

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.340
in order to report
clinical trials.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:11.380
So one of my main
jobs today is actually

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.210
just writing a lot
of our packages

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.130
for our specific needs.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:18.970
Pharma does a lot of things
that are very pharma,

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.160
that are just like, if it--

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:24.220
whether it comes from
doing things like the way

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.070
we format tables
and create tables.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:29.320
Pharma does stuff that most--

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.720
most of the times, you
don't do things like--

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.820
just in the world of
tables, because that's

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.090
my most recent package.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.560
So I can talk all about
tables and table design

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.460
as interesting and exciting
as that is to anybody--

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:46.450
is things like we tend
to make mock tables.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.250
We make a fake version
of the table we

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:52.390
want before we have any data.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:56.890
And then we use
that fake version

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:00.385
to make the table we want
much later down the line.

00:04:00.385 --> 00:04:02.260
But oftentimes, the fake
version of the table

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.110
happens six months to
a year or even more,

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:08.600
depending on how long your
study is to making that table.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.370
So doing things that make
it so that it's easier

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:16.060
to work through
the pharma pipeline

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:19.930
and allow for automation
while making our packages

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:23.890
is basically my job, which is
really long winded way to say,

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:25.630
I make our packages.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:28.205
But that is what I do.

00:04:28.205 --> 00:04:29.830
And I think that was
