00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:10.700
So I'm in a pretty small team.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.190
There are four of us on my team.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:20.560
And we do the modularity-ish
of the package building here

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:25.880
at GSK at least for our internal
use and to some external ones.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.550
There are other people
in our community

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:32.530
who help with other projects
like the Admiral project--

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:33.560
an admiral package.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.110
There are people in our
department who do that,

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.560
but I am not one
of those people.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.070
I do other pharmaverse things.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:42.430
I currently hold--
within the pharmaverse,

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.460
I'm the person who writes
packages to deal with metadata.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:47.620
I don't know how this
has become my life.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:49.570
It was an accident.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.000
It wasn't like I love metadata.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.480
So I have three primary
packages that I maintain

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.140
within the pharmaverse,
metacore which

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:03.790
deals with metadata
around data sets,

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:08.290
metatools which uses that
metadata to do fun automation

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:12.310
stuff, and t-format which deals
with metadata around formatting

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:12.940
tables.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:15.760
So that's all of
the metadata I hold

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:19.690
in my world of
pharma-based metadata.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:23.390
But that is-- so that's like me.

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:26.550
And then my team is really--

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:32.070
they're-- primarily me and
Becca Krauss who's on-- who does

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:37.020
safety graphics and [INAUDIBLE]
who does [INAUDIBLE]..

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:40.780
So there's-- all of us have
our own packages as well.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:45.630
But those are the ones
that we maintain right now.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:46.130
Cool.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.640
I think that was-- sorry,
